Subject: [PATCH v3 6/8] jails/instances/lab-mail: Refuse malformed posts
To: Pat Maddox <pat@patmaddox.com>
Cc: lab-devel@p7x.dev
Change-Id: luzwntuvsutlnzvsmypnvrmunxwlwpru
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 08:40:33 +0000

Anyone who can reach lab-mail may post, and every post lands on the
list for all of its readers. A message with a broken header, or
without exactly one From, Subject, and Message-ID, breaks threading
and the tools that read the list. Refused at the end of DATA, it
never enters the queue, and the poster learns why while still
connected.

- check-message, an smtpd-filters(7) filter in awk, refuses such a
  message with a 550 reply that names the fault.
- OpenSMTPD runs it on the listener, as nobody.
